Continuity — a voice-based health companion designed to help elderly patients maintain a continuous record of their health between doctor visits.

The idea is simple: instead of asking patients to remember weeks of symptoms, Continuity remembers for them.

Each day, the patient has a short, natural voice check-in. 

Based on their known condition, Continuity asks condition-specific questions, similar to what a doctor would normally ask during a consultation.

It can also provide medication reminders and log adherence, without ever suggesting or changing medication dosages.

Over time, these conversations build a structured health history.

And before an appointment, Continuity turns that history into a clear, doctor-ready report, highlighting symptoms, trends, medication adherence, and important follow-up notes.

So the patient doesn't have to remember everything at the appointment — their health history is already ready for them.
